],[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-2 flex items-baseline justify-between gap-x-3 gap-y-1 flex-wrap\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline gap-2.5 text-sm md:text-base font-heading font-semibold text-text-primary uppercase tracking-[0.06em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-block rounded-sm px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.16em] self-center\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#4dc9f6\",\"background\":\"#4dc9f61a\",\"border\":\"1px solid #4dc9f640\"},\"children\":\"Legend\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankCardH3\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Terizla\",\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L40\",null,{\"href\":\"/tier-list?rank=legend\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-text-accent hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankTierListLink\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}],\" →\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-muted text-[13px] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceLead\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\",\"name\":\"Terizla\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"51.79\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Terizla\",\"delta\":\"+0.94%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.34\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.24\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[\"$La0\",\"$La1\",\"$La2\"]}],\"$La3\",\"$La4\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The pick test is stricter than players admit. If you cannot name the ally who follows your ultimate, Terizla is already shaky. If the enemy has two heroes who can reset your spacing on demand, he is probably wrong.\"}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Terizla works when one patch of ground stops being safe\"]}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Terizla is not a bruiser in the normal sense. He is a bad-place generator.\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"His passive is the reason. As his HP drops, he gets harder to remove, and every attack-speed bonus he would have gained gets converted into physical attack instead. That tells you almost everything about how he should be played. Terizla does not want attack-speed gimmicks, hit-and-run trades, or long chases across open space. He wants one controlled area where the enemy has to decide whether to eat the slow, eat the pull, or burn movement just to avoid the third swing.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"That is why the rest of the kit fits together so cleanly. Revenge Strike is the tag that starts the walk-down. Execution Strike is the real test, because the first two swings ask whether the target can still leave and the third swing punishes the wrong answer. Penalty Zone exists to remove the easiest answer of all, which is simply walking out before the full sequence lands.\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Read him that way and most bad decisions disappear. You stop asking whether Terizla can flank like an assassin. He cannot. You stop asking whether he should split the map alone after mid game. Usually no. You start asking one better question instead: can this fight be forced to happen inside his cone and his hook zone long enough for the enemy carry to panic?\"}]\n84:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Laning: the first four minutes\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Start S2 and spend the full cast on the wave.\"}],\" Since the mana removal, there is no reward for half-committing the first wave just to save resources. Use all three swings if that is what it takes to win lane priority, clip the enemy EXP laner if he stands too close, and make the second wave arrive on your terms.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Hold S1 until the opponent has already shown movement.\"}],\" Revenge Strike is much stronger after a dash than before one. If you throw it first, better EXP laners sidestep, reset, and walk back in after your only clean leash is gone. If you tag them after they spend movement, the slow and your speed-up decide whether the trade continues.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Spend battle-spell tempo on the first Turtle fight, not on lane ego.\"}],\" If you brought \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/spells\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Flicker\"}],\", keep it for the first real catch angle around river or the jungle mouth. If you brought \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-1\",{\"href\":\"/spells\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Vengeance\"}],\", save it for the trade where the enemy marksman or fighter has no choice but to hit you back. Terizla wins when his spell changes an objective fight, not when it cashes one low-value solo kill.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The lane plan is simple. Get control of the first two waves, keep enough HP to walk first toward the crab or Turtle side, and force the enemy EXP laner to decide whether he wants to contest your wave or your body. Terizla does not need a flashy solo kill to win early game. He needs first access.\"}]\n87:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The two-item spike that makes him honest\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"The default spike is \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/items/war-axe\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"War Axe\"}],\" plus \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-1\",{\"href\":\"/items/queens-wings\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Queen's Wings\"}]]}],\", usually around the 7 to 9 minute mark in an even game.\"]}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"War Axe gives Terizla the exact shape of stats he wants for extended contact: HP, cooldown reduction, spell vamp, and damage that keeps rewarding him if the fight lasts longer than one button press. Terizla stacks it naturally because his real fights are never one clean burst. They are S1 tag, first hammer, second hammer, third hammer, then one more step forward while the target tries to leave.\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Queen's Wings is the partner because it turns his passive from annoying into expensive. The extra spell vamp, the low-HP damage reduction, and the cooldown refund all reward the same thing: staying inside the brawl instead of backing out after one rotation. Once both items are online, Terizla stops feeling like a lane bully with a teamfight ult and starts feeling like a real first body into the choke.\"}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"There is one honest exception. If the enemy lane or front line depends on shield or HP regen to survive, \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/items/dominance-ice\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Dominance Ice\"}],\" can replace Queen's Wings as the second item and the game still makes sense. But that is a matchup tax, not the baseline identity. The default Terizla spike is War Axe plus Queen's Wings because that is the moment his full commit actually pays.\"]}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"$La5\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n8d:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight positioning and target priority\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The wrong reflex is to Flicker past the front line because you saw a highlight clip once. That turns Terizla into a slow assassin with no exit and no second cast window.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Start at the first body in the choke, not the dream carry in the back.\"}],\" Terizla is strongest when the front line and back line get trapped in the same decision tree. If you start on the first hero who steps into bad ground, the hooks and slows force the carry to either walk closer or abandon the fight.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Cast S2 after the zone starts doing work.\"}],\" Penalty Zone is valuable because it compresses movement options. If you start swinging before the pulls force that movement, the first hammer lands where the enemy used to be. Let the zone pin the path first, then aim the cone at the only exit left.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Aim the third swing at the escape route, not the current model.\"}],\" This is where most Terizla damage disappears. The third hit is the reason the sequence matters. Re-angle between casts. Step forward. If the enemy is escaping toward tower, brush, or jungle mouth, the third slam belongs there.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Target priority is front-to-back unless the enemy gifts you something cleaner. Hit the highest-value target who cannot fully leave your sequence. Sometimes that is the tank. Sometimes it is the mage who stood one step too near the first engage. Terizla does not need the perfect carry catch to win a fight. He needs one target whose exit path has already become expensive.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Support-dependent edge case: if your support is Mathilda or Angela, you can take a greedier first step because both cover the ugly second after you land. If your support is Estes or Floryn, do the opposite. Fight in front of them, make the enemy walk into your cone, and stop pretending you are the flank.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8